.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-modules 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-modules \- Measure the crate\*(Aqs module graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten modules\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Measure the crate\*(Aqs module graph
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-modules\-cycle(1)
Print how many modules the largest cycle of the module graph holds, refusing more than \-\-max
.TP
batten\-modules\-impls(1)
Print how many inherent impls sit away from their type\*(Aqs module, refusing more than \-\-max
.TP
batten\-modules\-shims(1)
Print how many re\-exports of the crate\*(Aqs own items sit outside its root, refusing more than \-\-max
.TP
batten\-modules\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
